  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Energy Sector Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sierra Leone Compact - Energy Sector Project: The Transmission Backbone Project will seek to increase coverage and reliability of the transmission network with modern, centralized system operations. The project includes major investments in centralized control and a new transmission corridor as well as investments in the network to ensure continuity of service during and after the construction of compact investments. The proposed national dispatch center and associated supervisory control and data acquisition (SCADA) upgrades will improve the utilities&#xfffd; capabilities to manage an increasingly complex grid&#xfffd;facilitating quicker responses to network disruptions, improved integration of variable and renewable generation sources, and stronger regional integration with neighboring countries. The proposed construction of a southern transmission corridor will help eliminate an existing transmission bottleneck as well as support longer-term demand growth and grid expansion to southern parts of the country.</narrative>
  </description>
